Subject: [PATCH 03/23] llama : direct safetensors loading (M3) + fp8 perf
 fixes

- new src/llama-safetensors.h/.cpp: parse config.json + safetensors
  headers, mmap weights, synthesize gguf metadata, tensor data callback
- llama_model_load_from_file auto-detects safetensors dirs/files
- D3 hardware gate: fp8 requires a native-FP8 device, full offload
- transforms ported from conversion/qwen.py (V-head reorder, fp8
  re-blocking, +1 norms, A_log -exp, MTP mapping); F32 output types
  for 1D/norm/conv1d tensors per conversion/base.py
- llama-model-loader: metadata-only path fixes (get_weight fallback,
  NOT_REQUIRED skip semantics, TENSOR_SKIP handling)
- fp8.cu: host-side RDNA4 dispatch was compiled out by a device-only
  #if guard (silent scalar fallback); dot4 GEMV path for n <= 16;
  GLU fusion excludes F8 (mmvq abort)
- perf: generation 3.2 -> 72.5 t/s on 1x R9700 (Q8_0 baseline 91.7)

